# AJ-E2011 (ENGINEERING-GUIDE A3, T1, I3, I4): today's commands that break an
# IPC rule, by rule. This list only shrinks: fix a command and drop its line.
# Format: <rule> <command>   (rules: uncalled, sync, main-thread, unbounded, long, name)
# sync and main-thread are empty (0.1.5 review: a sync command runs on the
# main thread, and a page that asked for one froze the window): every
# command is async. A command that must run on the main thread is marked
# `// ipc: main-thread (why)` and listed here as `main-thread <command>  # why`.
# unbounded (2026-10-25): a command whose list can grow pages it (paging.rs);
# each listed one says why its list stays small, or "TO PAGE" with what reads it.
# uncalled entries carry the date they were listed: 2026-10-21.
uncalled account_audit
uncalled harnesses_list_alias
uncalled isolation_check
uncalled parked_list
uncalled pricing_catalog_info
uncalled pricing_override_clear
uncalled pricing_override_set
uncalled profiles_list_alias
uncalled recommendation_for
uncalled scan_cancel
uncalled sessions_list_alias
uncalled usage_source_health
uncalled validation_dogfood_record
